# Implementation Plan - Expand UI Prototype

This plan outlines the creation of the remaining sections of the SIMAD oLearn Student Dashboard to provide a complete interactive prototype.

## Goal Description
Build fully functional HTML/CSS pages for the sidebar navigation items: **Courses**, **Exams**, **Calendar**, and **Support**. Connect them all via the existing sidebar for a seamless browsing experience.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> I will use the existing [styles.css](file:///Users/drshuunac/.gemini/antigravity/brain/133fe670-3110-434e-87dc-8bb99d00a8da/ui_prototype/styles.css) as the base, adding new specific classes for the calendar grid and complex tables as needed.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. New Pages
I will create the following files in `ui_prototype/`:

#### [NEW] ui_prototype/courses.html
*   **Grid View**: Expanded view of all enrolled courses.
*   **Course Details**: Progress bar, Grade to date, "Access" button.
*   **Tabs**: Active, Completed, Archived.

#### [NEW] ui_prototype/exams.html
*   **Table View**: List of upcoming and past exams.
*   **Status Indicators**: "Open", "Upcoming", "Closed".
*   **Action**: "Launch" button for active exams (links to Exam Shield mock logic).

#### [NEW] ui_prototype/calendar.html
*   **Grid**: Standard monthly view.
*   **Events**: Color-coded dots for Assignments (Blue), Exams (Red), Live Classes (Green).

#### [NEW] ui_prototype/support.html
*   **FAQ Section**: Accordion style.
*   **Ticket Form**: Input fields for Issue Type, Description, Attachment.
*   **History**: List of past tickets.

### 2. Updates
#### [MODIFY] ui_prototype/styles.css
*   Add styles for `table`, `tabs`, `calendar-grid`, and `form-elements`.

#### [MODIFY] ui_prototype/index.html & All Pages
*   Update sidebar `href` attributes to point to the correct HTML files.
*   Ensure the "Active" class works on the correct sidebar item for each page.

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
*   **Navigation Check**: Click through every sidebar link in the browser loop (`localhost:8000`) to ensure no broken links.
*   **Visual Consistency**: Ensure headers, sidebars, and fonts match across all pages.
